on":"Behind-the-scenes enhancement. Formerly called “core”.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2026-08-18T08:24:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T07:44:08Z","closed_at":"2026-10-06T07:44:08Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/5526","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/5526","diff_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/5526.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/5526.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-06T07:44:08Z"},"body":"Issue described in https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/5462#issuecomment-5313700120 is actually not specific to `TabsPanel`, it is a global issue. hence fixed in `useId` instead of patching as suggested by `codex review`.\r\n\r\n## Issue\r\n\r\nOn React 17, a component that mounted with an `id` prop kept that id forever, removing the prop never fell back to a generated one, because the fallback stored the caller's id in the slot meant for generated ids. Also switches `||` to `??` so an empty-string `id` is respected.\r\n\r\nNew `useId.react17.test.tsx` forces the fallback branch (mocks `SafeReact.useId` to `undefined`), which nothing tested before since the repo runs React 19 and CI's oldest job is React 18.\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5526/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}